  "body": "First slice of #1449: a 2D Pocket can enter each level by a straight plunge down a hole that a Drill operation ahead of it in the same setup made. It does this only where that hole is proved open. Everything else keeps the asked helix, ramp or arc, and the path says why by name.\n\nBranched from upstream/main at ba3776b1 (the mkinney fork's main is on v0.18.0; this branch carries upstream's current process files).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`camcraft-motion`**\n  - New `Approach::predrilled` flag (default off).\n  - New `machining2d::predrilled` module and `pocket_entered(region, params, holes)`; `pocket()` is unchanged and calls it with no holes.\n  - The ladder's `descent::plan` takes a proved hole ahead of every arm. A hole is used only when it is open to the level's Z, its centre is a legal cutter centre, and the dive link from it to the pass start is proved. When no hole serves a level, the asked entry stands and a note says why.\n  - The pass plan is re-seated on the deepest proved hole: a ring is rotated, an open zigzag pass is split into a forward tail and a reversed head. The link from the hole is then the shortest one to any pass, so it crosses none (verify's Crossing law stays silent).\n- **`camcraft-app`**\n  - New `operation::predrilled_entry::proved_holes`. Hole centres come from the moves of the Drill ops ahead (`rest::drills_ahead`, now also collected for a Pocket with the flag on). A hole is kept only if:\n    - the drill's stated diameter is at least the tool's + 2 x 0.1 mm clearance;\n    - the prior grid (the stock the program ahead leaves, as the drilling and thread laws read it) holds no material over the tool disc + clearance above the counted depth;\n    - the counted depth is the deeper of the grid reading and the drill point's cone at the disc radius.\n  - Unprovable cases are named and the hole is left out: no drill, a drill too narrow (with the numbers), an unreadable prior, a posed 3+2 pocket.\n  - File: `links.approach.predrilled` (written only when on). Stamp: byte `0xC7` only when on. The pocket already goes Stale when the program ahead changes.\n  - Door: the flag on any kind other than 2D Pocket is refused by name (`PREDRILLED_POCKET_ONLY`), never silently dropped.\n- **Command / MCP:** the flag is an ordinary params field, so `EditOperationParams` (undoable) and MCP `edit_operation` / `add_operation` set it with `{\"links\": {\"approach\": {\"predrilled\": true}}}`. No new command or tool was needed.\n- **Decision:** `docs/decisions/1449-predrilled-entry.md`.\n\n## How tested (pins, each mutation-checked)\n\n| Pin | Test(s) | Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Hole proved: plunge at every level, no helix; posted G-code has `G00 X0 Y0 Z..` then `G01 X0 Y0 Z12 F200`; verify silent; posts through the gate | app `a_drilled_hole_ahead_is_plunged_to_full_depth_and_posted`, motion `a_proved_hole_is_plunged_at_every_level_with_no_helix` | entry never plunges | caught |\n| Delete the drill: the pocket goes Stale at once; regenerated, it has no plunge and uses the helix | app `deleting_the_drill_takes_the_plunge_away`, `without_the_drill_the_helix_stands_and_says_why` | pocket stamp ignores the program ahead | caught |\n| Hole the grid does not show is never air | unit `a_hole_the_grid_does_not_show_is_never_air`, `an_unreadable_prior_proves_nothing` | floor from drill moves only, grid dropped | caught |\n| Drill narrower than tool + clearance (Ø4 into Ø4, 4.2 needed): left out by name | app `a_drill_no_wider_than_the_tool_plus_clearance_is_refused_by_name`, unit twin | width check dropped | caught |\n| Shallow hole: only the levels it reaches plunge; the floor level helixes, named with the Z numbers | app + motion `a_shallow_hole_serves_only_the_levels_it_reaches` | depth check dropped | caught |\n| Hole outside the cutter-centre area is never plunged | motion `a_hole_outside_the_cutter_area_is_never_plunged` | area AND link proof dropped together | caught |\n| Area check alone (`predrilled.rs` entry filter) | unit `predrilled::tests::a_hole_outside_the_cutter_area_is_refused_even_at_the_pass_start` | area check dropped | caught (only this pin) |\n| Link proof alone | unit `predrilled::tests::a_hole_whose_link_crosses_a_planned_pass_is_refused` | link proof dropped | caught (only this pin) |\n| Non-centre-cutting tool keeps its entry, named | motion `a_tool_that_is_not_centre_cutting_keeps_the_asked_entry` | guard dropped | caught |\n| Undo/redo, file round trip, refused on another kind; MCP set + undo + refusal on adaptive | app `the_flag_is_an_undoable_edit_and_refused_off_the_pocket`, `mcp_sets_and_undoes_the_flag` | - | - |\n\nAlso: `with_the_flag_off_the_drill_is_never_read`, `without_a_hole_or_the_flag_the_helix_stands`, `a_non_finite_hole_is_ignored`, `a_posed_pocket_and_no_drill_are_named`, `an_open_wide_hole_is_handed_over_to_its_cone_depth`.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, head 9d098fe8): green - motion suites 140 s, app suites 691 s, ui suites 18 s, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean (without `--no-deps` the newer clippy flags three pre-existing `needless_range_loop` sites in the untouched `camcraft-geometry` feature.rs).\n\n## Not exercised / remaining on #1449\n\n- UI: no \"Entry positions (pre-drilled)\" group yet, so no structural UI test for it. The flag is reachable by MCP, script params and the file.\n- 2D Adaptive, Slot and the 3D roughing kinds (refused by name at the door for now).\n- Holes in the model, typed points with an explicit \"the hole exists\" choice, carried stock from a previous setup, and a \"pre-drilled only\" refusal mode.\n- Non-centre-cutting tools down a hole: the plunge law would need the proved holes.\n- A user-set clearance (fixed at 0.1 mm a side).\n- Golden CL file: the pins assert the moves and the posted lines directly.\n- No hand check in the GUI or on a machine.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket: pre-drilled entry - with `links.approach.predrilled` on, each level is entered by a straight plunge down a hole a Drill operation ahead of it in the setup made, only where the stock simulation proves the hole open wide and deep enough; elsewhere the asked entry stands, named (#1449, first slice)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nRefs #1449\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n\n",
